{"id":87,"text":"Long ago, a traveller crossing a vast desert noticed a small green plant growing between two enormous rocks. He knelt down and looked at it with amazement. There was no water for miles, and the heat was brutal.\n\nA nomad who was passing by stopped beside him. “Everyone is surprised by that plant,” he said. “Do you know its story?”\n\n“Please tell me,” said the traveller.\n\n“Years ago, a seed fell here during a rare storm,” said the nomad. “It had only a few drops of water, which was enough for a tiny root. For months, it grew downward, not upward. The root searched for deep water, ignoring the scorching surface. Only when it had found moisture did a small shoot appear.”\n\nThe traveller looked at the plant again. It was thin and humble, but alive.\n\n“Most people want to grow upward immediately,” said the nomad. “They want success and recognition fast. But in difficult places, the ones who survive are those who first build deep roots.”\n\nThe traveller thought about his own life. He had always rushed to show results, but he had never asked what supported him from below. That evening, as the sun set over the dunes, he decided to spend less time impressing others and more time strengthening himself.\n\nMoral: In hard times, growth begins underground, so build deep roots before you reach for the sky.","tr":null,"gl":{"long":"uzoq, uzun","ago":"oldin, ilgari","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","traveller":"sayyoh","crossing":"o'tish","vast":"keng, ulkan","desert":"cho'l","noticed":"payqadi","small":"kichik","green":"yashil","plant":"ekmoq; o'simlik","growing":"o'sayotgan","between":"orasida","two":"ikki","enormous":"juda ulkan","rocks":"toshlar","he":"u (erkak)","knelt":"tiz cho'kdi","down":"pastga","and":"va","looked":"qaradi","at":"-da, -ga","it":"u (narsa)","with":"bilan","amazement":"hayrat","there":"u yerda; bor","was":"edi","no":"yo'q; hech qanday","water":"suv; sug'ormoq","for":"uchun; davomida","miles":"mil (masofa)","the":"(aniq artikl)","heat":"issiq